@startuml fleet-shell-layout
title Fleet shell: panel arrangement (B2)

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
}

rectangle "Top bar\nworkspace | back/forward | context line | Smart Mode / Problems / branch" as Top
rectangle "Left rail\n(Project icon)" as LeftRail
rectangle "Project tool window\n(slim tree)" as Tree
rectangle "Central panel\ntabs + editor  (or Source Control view)" as Center
rectangle "Right rail\n(Claude icon)" as RightRail
rectangle "Claude tool window" as Claude
rectangle "Bottom rail\n(Find/Run/Problems icons)" as BottomRail
rectangle "Bottom tool window\nProblems | Cargo Output | Usages | Search" as Bottom
rectangle "Status bar\nline:col | encoding | EOL | indent | errors/warnings | branch" as Status

Top -[hidden]down- LeftRail
LeftRail -right- Tree
Tree -right- Center
Center -right- RightRail
RightRail -right- Claude
Center -[hidden]down- BottomRail
BottomRail -down- Bottom
Bottom -[hidden]down- Status

note bottom of Status
  Zen Mode hides everything except Central panel.
  Tool-window flags (Project/Claude/Bottom) hide only
  that window's content -- its rail icon stays visible
  either way, so it can be reopened.
end note
@enduml
